- Ec2 estimated cost is approximately $4/month for a t2.nano instance running continously. 
- AWS Lambda costs $0 per 1 million requests

- Break-even point:
EC2 cost (4) divided by labda cost per 1 M requests = 40 million requests per month.

- Lambda becomes more expensive than EC2 only after approximately 40 million requests per month.
- However bellow threshold, lambda is cheaper for this workload